Title: RACOON RESCUE - V2
Credit: Scene Draft
Author: Scene Writer Agent
Draft date: January 2026

===

/* THE HEIST - Danny captures the raccoon */
/* Approximate page count: 2-2.5 pages */
/* Three-act structure: Reconnaissance / Approach / Extraction */
/* Tone: Ocean's Eleven-ing a garbage animal */

EXT. DUSTY'S PARKING LOT - DUMPSTER - NIGHT

Danny straightens up. Squares his shoulders. The drunk sway
in his stance steadies into something else.

Purpose.

He circles the dumpster. Slow. Measured. A predator assessing
terrain. Three steps left. Pause. Listen. Three steps right.

His eyes sweep the perimeter. The back door of Dusty's: closed.
The parking lot: empty. The distant highway: cars passing,
indifferent, their headlights sweeping the tree line.

Danny stops. Reaches down. Picks up a PEBBLE.

He weighs it in his palm. Rolls it between his fingers.

Tosses it into the dumpster.

PLINK.

He waits.

Nothing. No movement. No chittering. Just the slow rhythm of
a belly rising and falling among the trash.

Danny nods. Good recon.

He moves to his TRUCK. Opens the door. Pulls out a WORK JACKET--
heavy canvas, the kind meant for welding or crawling under
engines.

He shrugs it on. Buttons it to the collar.

Rolls up the sleeves. Once. Twice. Tight against his forearms.

Flexes his fingers. Cracks his knuckles.

The gesture is ridiculous. The execution is flawless.

He approaches the dumpster again. Stops at the edge. Places
both hands on the rim.

LOW ANGLE: Danny peers over the edge into darkness. The sodium
vapor light catches his face from below. He looks like a man
about to defuse a bomb.

DANNY
(under his breath)
Okay. Okay.

He looks left. Right. Back at the dumpster.

DANNY (CONT'D)
Easy.

He pulls himself up. Swings one leg over. Then the other.

He DISAPPEARS into the dumpster.

EXT. DUSTY'S PARKING LOT - WIDE SHOT - CONTINUOUS

The dumpster sits in its pool of orange light. Silent.

Then:

DANNY (O.S.)
(muffled)
Oh god.

A CLANG from inside. Something shifts.

DANNY (O.S.) (CONT'D)
Oh god what is that smell--

More shifting. The dumpster ROCKS slightly on its wheels.

DANNY (O.S.) (CONT'D)
Okay. Okay okay okay--

Silence.

A long beat.

DANNY (O.S.) (CONT'D)
(barely audible)
Come here. Come here, buddy.

The dumpster lid BANGS open.

DANNY emerges.

He stands in the dumpster, cradling something against his
chest. Both arms wrapped around it. Protective. Tender.

THE RACCOON.

It hangs limp in his arms. Fat belly. Tiny paws dangling. A
smear of something--ketchup? barbecue sauce?--across its fur.

Danny's face is RADIANT. The joy of a man who has done something
impossible. Who has solved the unsolvable. Who has stolen fire
from the gods.

He climbs out of the dumpster. One leg, then the other. Careful.
So careful. Like the creature in his arms might shatter.

Something DRIPS from his jacket. He does not look down.

He walks toward the truck. His gait has changed. No longer the
swagger of a drunk. The measured steps of a man carrying
precious cargo.

EXT. DANNY'S TRUCK - CONTINUOUS

Danny reaches the driver's side door. Looks down at the
raccoon. At his arms, full of sleeping wildlife.

He cannot open the door.

He stands there. Calculating. Processing. Too drunk to have
planned this far ahead.

Slowly, he shifts the raccoon to one arm. Cradles it like a
football. Reaches for the door handle--

The raccoon STIRS.

Danny FREEZES.

The world stops. The sodium lights hum. A car passes on the
distant highway, its headlights sweeping across nothing.

The raccoon's nose TWITCHES. One paw flexes. Relaxes.

Its eyes stay closed.

Danny does not breathe.

One second. Two. Three.

The raccoon's head lolls. It settles deeper into the crook of
his arm. Returns to its garbage coma.

Danny exhales.

He YANKS the door open. THROWS himself into the truck. Pulls
the door shut with his elbow. All in one motion. Explosive.
Desperate.

INT. DANNY'S TRUCK - CONTINUOUS

Danny sits behind the wheel. Breathing hard. The raccoon in
his lap, still unconscious.

He looks down at it. Then at the BREATHALYZER INTERLOCK. The
red LED eye, waiting.

Danny lifts the raccoon's head. Positions its muzzle near the
breathalyzer tube.

He pauses.

DANNY
(whispered)
Don't wake up. Don't you dare
wake up.

He squeezes the raccoon's belly.

The raccoon EXHALES into the tube.

Danny watches the LED.

Waits.

BEEP.

GREEN.

The ENGINE turns over.

Danny stares at the raccoon. The raccoon sleeps on. Oblivious
to its role in the crime of the century.

Danny puts the truck in gear.

EXT. DUSTY'S PARKING LOT - NIGHT

The pickup pulls out of its space. Headlights sweep across
the empty lot.

The dumpster stands alone. Lid still open. Missing something
it never knew it had.

The truck turns onto the highway. Disappears into the dark.

FADE TO BLACK.

/* End scene - approximately 2.25 pages */
/* Note: The humor must come from Danny's SERIOUSNESS */
/* Every beat played straight. The absurdity speaks for itself. */
